# `module::Chord::validate`

[Back to `module::Chord`](../Chord.md)

Validates every asset and reports all problems together, each naming its asset.

## Signature

```cpp
void module::Chord::validate() const;
```

## What It Does

Runs the validation of [`Field::validate`](../../field/Field/validate.md) on every asset and throws one error that lists the problems of all the failing assets, each starting `asset 'name'`. Assets that are fine are not mentioned, so a book can be corrected in one pass instead of one error at a time. [`price`](price.md), [`implied_vol`](implied_vol.md) and `simulate_paths` validate first, so a book that passes `validate` can be priced.

Call it after assembling or editing a book, before a long calculation, or to give a user every mistake at once. An empty Chord has nothing to validate and passes.

## Returns

Nothing.

## Errors

Throws `subsp::math::finance::module::Chord:` followed by one line per failing asset, `asset '<name>': ...`, with the Field's own message; an asset with several problems lists each on its own indented line, headed `(<n> problems)`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1: a valid chord passes silently

No output and no exception.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static mod::Field bs(double spot, double strike, double vol, double maturity = 1.0) {
  return mod::Field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, strike, maturity), .market = fin::market::make(spot, 0.02, 0.01),
                    .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})}, .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Analytic}};
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(5));
  mod::Chord chord;
  chord.add("a", bs(100.0, 100.0, 0.20)).add("b", bs(90.0, 95.0, 0.30));
  chord.validate();
  out.writeln("valid");
}
```

### Example 2: one bad asset among good ones

Only the failing asset is named.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static mod::Field bs(double spot, double strike, double vol, double maturity = 1.0) {
  return mod::Field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, strike, maturity), .market = fin::market::make(spot, 0.02, 0.01),
                    .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})}, .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Analytic}};
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(5));
  const auto report = [&](const auto &call) {
    try {
      call();
    } catch (const std::exception &e) {
      std::string text(e.what());
      if (const auto cut = text.find("Triggered"); cut != std::string::npos) text.erase(cut);
      while (!text.empty() && text.back() == '\n') text.pop_back();
      out.writeln(text);
    }
  };
  mod::Chord chord;
  chord.add("fine", bs(100.0, 100.0, 0.20)).add("negative spot", bs(-1.0, 100.0, 0.20));
  report([&] { chord.validate(); });
}
```

### Example 3: every failing asset in one message

Two failing assets are reported together, the second with both of its problems.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static mod::Field bs(double spot, double strike, double vol, double maturity = 1.0) {
  return mod::Field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, strike, maturity), .market = fin::market::make(spot, 0.02, 0.01),
                    .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})}, .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Analytic}};
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(5));
  const auto report = [&](const auto &call) {
    try {
      call();
    } catch (const std::exception &e) {
      std::string text(e.what());
      if (const auto cut = text.find("Triggered"); cut != std::string::npos) text.erase(cut);
      while (!text.empty() && text.back() == '\n') text.pop_back();
      out.writeln(text);
    }
  };
  mod::Chord chord;
  chord.add("fine", bs(100.0, 100.0, 0.20)).add("negative spot", bs(-1.0, 100.0, 0.20)).add("zero strike and vol", bs(100.0, 0.0, 0.0));
  report([&] { chord.validate(); });
}
```

### Example 4: an empty chord

There is nothing to check, so it passes.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(5));
  mod::Chord chord;
  chord.validate();
  out.writeln("an empty chord is valid");
}
```

### Example 5: price validates first

`price` throws the same report instead of pricing the assets that are fine.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static mod::Field bs(double spot, double strike, double vol, double maturity = 1.0) {
  return mod::Field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, strike, maturity), .market = fin::market::make(spot, 0.02, 0.01),
                    .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})}, .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Analytic}};
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(5));
  const auto report = [&](const auto &call) {
    try {
      call();
    } catch (const std::exception &e) {
      std::string text(e.what());
      if (const auto cut = text.find("Triggered"); cut != std::string::npos) text.erase(cut);
      while (!text.empty() && text.back() == '\n') text.pop_back();
      out.writeln(text);
    }
  };
  mod::Chord chord;
  chord.add("fine", bs(100.0, 100.0, 0.20)).add("negative spot", bs(-1.0, 100.0, 0.20));
  report([&] { (void)chord.price(); });
}
```

